      "program_name": "Monterey County Housing Trust Fund (MCHTF) loans for affordable rental development",
      "administering_agency": "Monterey County Housing and Community Development Department",
      "funding_type": "loan",
      "typical_award_size": "Established May 17, 2022 (Resolution 22-100) to replace redevelopment set-aside; by April 2023 the County had committed $10,033,984 of local cash, land assets and PLHA to capitalize it, including about $420,000 of PLHA delegated by Carmel-by-the-Sea, Greenfield and Soledad plus about $289,000 a year from those cities' later allocations. Loans: Greenfield Commons (EAH Housing, 100 units, Greenfield) $1,929,046 ($1,028,833 trust fund plus $900,213 PLHA) approved March 2023 and increased by $550,000 trust fund plus $9,982 PLHA on December 22, 2025 for cost overruns; Lightfighter Village (EAH and Veterans Transition Center, 71 units, Marina) $500,115. Loan origination fee corrected to 0.5%. The County applied to the state Local Housing Trust Fund matching program in 2022 (unsuccessful) and 2023 (up to $5 million match on $3,544,645 eligible local funds); a 2024 Board referral explored using 1220 Natividad Road to recapitalize the fund.",
      "per_unit_cap": "Not published; awards of $500,000 to $2.5 million per project (about $5,000 to $25,000 per unit).",
      "affordability_requirement": "Lower income rental housing with 55-year County regulatory agreements; LHTF rules (3% simple maximum, predevelopment, acquisition, construction and permanent loans) when matched by state funds.",
      "eligible_project_types": [
        "new construction",
        "acquisition-rehab",
        "supportive housing",
        "predevelopment"
      ],
      "application_cycle": "rolling",
      "next_deadline": "No standing NOFA; awards have gone by Board resolution to projects identified in the County's LHTF application. Contact HCD housing staff about trust fund and PLHA availability for 2027 tax credit applications; the pending inclusionary fee restructuring is intended to feed this fund.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "true",
      "layering_notes": "Monterey County's Housing and Community Development Department (HCD, Craig Spencer, Director; Darby Marshall, Housing Program Manager) runs the Inclusionary Housing Ordinance, the Monterey County Housing Trust Fund, PLHA, the Urban County CDBG and HOME programs and County land dispositions; the County Administrative Office Homelessness Strategies and Initiatives Division (CAO-HSI) runs HHAP and the SHARE Center; the Health Department Behavioral Health Bureau holds BHSA; the Coalition of Homeless Services Providers leads the CoC (CA-506, shared with San Benito); and the Housing Authority of the County of Monterey (HACM) and its Development Corporation supply vouchers and develop housing. Salinas, Monterey, Seaside and other entitlement cities run their own programs (Pass 3). countyofmonterey.gov blocks automated access (pages and documents), so records were built from the Legistar web API client 'monterey' and its Granicus attachments, hamonterey.org, chsp.org, zoneomics and HCD tables. The trust fund is the County's gap lender of record but is thinly capitalized (two projects to date); its future depends on inclusionary in-lieu fee revenue and PLHA delegations from small cities. Source is the December 22, 2025 Board item (Legistar file 26-009) with the Greenfield Commons loan resolutions; establishment and LHTF history from files RES 22-100 and RES 23-073.",
      "source_url": "https://monterey.legistar.com/LegislationDetail.aspx?ID=64104&GUID=BDC529D7-8D60-4518-9694-BC145F3D3E03",
      "record_id": "10e2bcb657",
      "cycle_notes": "",
      "eligible_project_detail": [
        "new construction multifamily rental",
        "veteran and supportive housing",
        "predevelopment and acquisition (LHTF-eligible)"
      ],
      "next_deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_check": "no_date",
      "link_status": "ok"
