      "typical_award_size": "First cycle (2019-2023) County estimate $3,890,280, raised to $5,631,969 after Carmel-by-the-Sea, Greenfield and Soledad delegated their allocations to the County in 2024; 2024-2028 formula allocations $455,119 (2024) and $487,499 (2025). Uses: rental development (Greenfield Commons $900,213 plus $9,982), homeless assistance passed to Social Services for the Salinas SHARE Center navigation center (up to $1,593,176) and case management ($790,275) through December 31, 2026, homeownership assistance, administration, and a $1,680,063 reserve for affordable owner-occupied workforce housing (AOWH) that the City of Soledad asked to use for a moderate-income for-sale land purchase (committee March 16, 2026). PLHA fund balance $1,191,927 at September 2026.",
