      "next_deadline": "No NOFA; PLHA is committed by Board resolution alongside Housing Trust Fund loans and by inter-departmental agreements for homeless services. The AOWH reserve is the only uncommitted development money identified; ask HCD about the 2026 and 2027 allocation years.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "true",
      "layering_notes": "Monterey County's Housing and Community Development Department (HCD, Craig Spencer, Director; Darby Marshall, Housing Program Manager) runs the Inclusionary Housing Ordinance, the Monterey County Housing Trust Fund, PLHA, the Urban County CDBG and HOME programs and County land dispositions; the County Administrative Office Homelessness Strategies and Initiatives Division (CAO-HSI) runs HHAP and the SHARE Center; the Health Department Behavioral Health Bureau holds BHSA; the Coalition of Homeless Services Providers leads the CoC (CA-506, shared with San Benito); and the Housing Authority of the County of Monterey (HACM) and its Development Corporation supply vouchers and develop housing. Salinas, Monterey, Seaside and other entitlement cities run their own programs (Pass 3). countyofmonterey.gov blocks automated access (pages and documents), so records were built from the Legistar web API client 'monterey' and its Granicus attachments, hamonterey.org, chsp.org, zoneomics and HCD tables. PLHA has been split between homeless operations (SHARE Center) and the trust fund's Greenfield Commons loan; a developer with an unincorporated or small-city project should ask for PLHA and trust fund money together. Source is the September 21, 2026 PLHA budget amendment item (Legistar file 26-831); Soledad request from file 26-261 and 2024-2028 figures from HCD's PLHA NOFA tables.",
